2. Certificates issued under the v31null TL
The certificates issued to natural persons (hereafter ‘v31null eIDs’) follow ETSI EN 319 412-2 V2.5.1. Their subject contains countryName PZ, the givenName and surname as indicated on the holder’s official identity document, the commonName, and, as serialNumber, the holder’s V31N Public PIN. PZ is not a code assigned in ISO 3166-1.

The key usage of a v31null eID is non-repudiation only (ETSI EN 319 412-2 V2.5.1, clause 4.3.2, type A). Its certificate policy is 0.4.0.2042.1.1 (ETSI EN 319 411-1 V1.5.1, NCP). The identity of the holder is verified by a registration officer of the V31N Help Desk against official documents.

The validity is 25 years for a root CA, 10 years for a subordinate CA and 2 years for a v31null eID. Certificate revocation lists are issued at least every 24 hours (ETSI EN 319 411-1 V1.5.1, CSS-6.3.9-05) and certification authority revocation lists at least once a year (CSS-6.3.9-12), at the URLs indicated in the certificates.

The cryptographic suites follow ETSI TS 119 312 V2.1.1. Signatures are validated according to ETSI EN 319 102-1 V1.4.1 and reported according to ETSI TS 119 102-2 V1.4.1.

The copies of personal data provided to account holders are sealed with the electronic seal of v31null (ETSI EN 319 412-3 V1.4.1). Its certificate is issued by the P-384 subordinate CA. Its subject contains countryName PZ, organizationName Mbrlí úír Entípatùíțù fùțbíz, organizationIdentifier 1 and commonName v31null nkz pik. Its key usage is non-repudiation only (type A), its certificate policy is 0.4.0.2042.1.1 and its validity is 10 years. A sealed copy is valid as information for 14 days from the time of sealing. The certificate is represented in PEM format in Annex 3 to this information, and can be authenticated using the following digest values:

